 "d": [
  {"i":4756,"keep":[1],"n":"Pencil lead (シャー芯) is a common stationery sense, so it fits the school unit"},
  {"i":4758,"keep":[],"n":"Following a plan or meeting expectations is not really the thinking unit; it is set-phrase usage"},
  {"i":4760,"keep":[2],"n":"Reflexes (反射神経) are a common physical sense that is taught with the body"},
  {"i":4761,"keep":[],"n":"Foot of a mountain is rare alone; learners usually meet it in 山裾 or 裾野"},
  {"i":4765,"keep":[],"n":"A clouded face is a figurative extension, and the weather sense covers the word"},
  {"i":4777,"keep":[2],"n":"Memories coming back (記憶が蘇る) is a very common sense and fits memory"},
  {"i":4782,"keep":[2],"n":"Being overwhelmed or deeply impressed (圧倒される) is common and emotional"},
  {"i":4806,"keep":[2],"n":"Saving a file is a core everyday tech sense"},
  {"i":4812,"keep":[],"n":"The fit/suit sense is less common and would not be taught under qualities"},
  {"i":4838,"keep":[2],"n":"Disability (障害者) is a common sense that belongs with health"},
  {"i":4846,"keep":[2],"n":"A clash of opinions (意見の衝突) is common and fits getting on with others"},
  {"i":4853,"keep":[2],"n":"Political or social pressure (圧力をかける) is a common sense in society contexts"},
  {"i":4865,"keep":[2],"n":"Bath and hot spring use (お湯に入る, 温泉の湯) is common for routine and travel"},
  {"i":4871,"keep":[1],"n":"Growing feelings (不安が募る) is a frequent sense and belongs to feelings"},
  {"i":4886,"keep":[],"n":"Dinner is normally 晩ご飯; 晩 alone meaning a meal is rare"},
  {"i":4887,"keep":[],"n":"小 for elementary school is only an abbreviation; learners learn 小学校"}
 ]
